  "type": "stepper_bipolar",
  "name": "Stepper motor (bipolar)",
  "category": "Motors & motion",
  "prefix": "M",
  "description": "Bipolar stepper motor like a NEMA 17: two coils (A+/A-, B+/B-) with their resistance and inductance; the rotor turns one step for each step of the coil currents (full, half or micro steps) and shows the shaft angle. Drive it with an H-bridge (L298) or a stepper driver; behavioral: no back EMF or inertia, so it never loses steps",
